codex
The J4 query uses only an upper bound on start position, so it scans the earlier chromosome prefix. I’ll add a lower bound derived from an indexed maximum footprint width. That preserves overlap semantics without hard-coding a length. J10 will verify J3’s `.done` and J9’s manifest before reading feature rows.

